1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,872
Movable Reality.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:05,038
Record your room and get a customizable 3D
room.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,468
All it needs is a video walkthrough from
the room and the ceiling height.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,352
No depth sensor, no floor plan,

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,320
no manual labelling.

6
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:17,431
Muse Wonder watches the video and lists
the objects.

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,356
SAM 3.1 tracks each one.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,247
MapAnything finds the cameras,

9
00:00:22,247 --> 00:00:24,798
and Gaussian splatting builds the room.

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:28,050
One command takes it from video to
finished room.

11
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:31,403
Every object comes out as its own set of
Gaussian splats.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,913
Select any,

13
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:34,718
move it along an axis,

14
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:35,650
or turn it.

15
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,600
Measure it.

16
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,639
Add furniture from a library.

17
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,319
Or just say what you want.

18
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,318
Ask it to move the sofa half of a metre,

19
00:00:45,318 --> 00:00:47,497
and it moves it thirty centimetres,

20
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,599
because the side table is in the way.

21
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,392
It answers questions too.

22
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,570
Will the armchair fit between the sofa and
the bookshelf?

23
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:55,737
No.

24
00:00:55,737 --> 00:00:58,621
The gap is one metre two, and the chair is
wider.

25
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:02,240
Ask for a plant, and it picks one and
places it.

26
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,200
After every edit,

27
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,513
Muse Spark Open looks at the room and
checks the result.

28
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:08,095
No walk sees everything.

29
00:01:08,095 --> 00:01:11,690
The pipeline scores what the video covered
and marks the spots

30
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:12,840
it barely saw.

31
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,740
The detail you get follows

32
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:15,934
the data you give it.

33
00:01:16,170 --> 00:01:17,570
This is a working demo,

34
00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:19,470
on two rooms rendered in Blender.

35
00:01:19,470 --> 00:01:22,666
It can be a good starting point for a
project or research.

36
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:24,720
Runs on eight Meta models.

37
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,520
It's MIT licensed,

38
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:29,620
each stage is a plain script you can swap,

39
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,590
and the test rooms and scoring tools come
with it,

40
00:01:32,590 --> 00:01:34,350
so you can measure your changes.

41
00:01:34,670 --> 00:01:36,468
Try the demo at the link below.
